8</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>HEALTH
AND SANITATION</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>UPDATED: 
March 30, 2022</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoTocHeading style='line-height:normal'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Chapter:</span></p>

<p class=MsoToc1 style='margin-left:45.0pt;text-indent:-45.0pt'><a href="#_Toc320001595"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>8.64</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;color:windowtext;text-decoration:none'>      </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>DISPOSITION OF REMAINS OF INDIGENT PERSONS</span></a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:45.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-45.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>CROSS REFERENCES:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Medical examiner see
K.C.C. chapter 2.24.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Surface and ground water
quality see K.C.C. chapter 9.12.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc320001595"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>8.64    DISPOSITION
OF REMAINS OF INDIGENT PERSONS</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          8.64.010     Definitions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          8.64.020     Policies.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          8.64.030     Procedures.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          8.64.040     Right of appeal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          8.64.010  Definitions.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
The following definitions shall apply in the interpretation and enforcement of
this chapter:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  &quot;Burial&quot;
means interment in a burial plot or an outer burial container, if required by
the cemetery authority, and the recording of related documents, including the
location of the remains.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  &quot;Cemetery
Authority&quot; means the owner or operator of a licensed cemetery.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  &quot;Cremation&quot;
means cremation and disposition of cremated remains, and recording of related
documents including the location of the remains.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  &quot;Crematory
Authority&quot; means the owner or operator of a licensed crematory.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  &quot;Disposition
of Remains&quot; means either burial or cremation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          F.  &quot;Estate&quot;
means all real and personal property of the decedent, including cash,
certificates of ownership or other tangible assets.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          G.  &quot;Funeral
Director&quot; means the owner or operator of a licensed funeral home.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          H.  &quot;Indigent&quot;
means a person who dies without leaving means sufficient to defray the expense
of disposition of the body.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          I.  &quot;Legally
Responsible Representative&quot; means the decedent's spouse, adult surviving
children, surviving parents, surviving siblings or a person acting as
representative of the decedent under the signed authorization of the decedent,
pursuant to RCW 68.50.160.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          J.  &quot;Manager&quot;
means the designee of the manager of the prevention division, Seattle-King
County department of public health.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          K.  &quot;Mortuary
Functions&quot; means first call and pick up of the decedent; transportation of
the decedent from the place of death to the mortuary and from the mortuary to a
cemetery or crematory; required care of the decedent for timely disposition in
compliance with State and local laws regarding care of dead human bodies, (e.g.
disinfecting and embalming or refrigeration); provision of a container, as prescribed
by law, for the transportation and, if necessary, the burial of the decedent;
retention of custody of cremated remains until disposition is determined;
disposition of cremated remains, if necessary; obtainment of authorization for
the disposition of remains and the use of county funds; and completion of the
death certificate.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          L.  &quot;Payment
Maximum Rates&quot; means the limit of payment the county will authorize for
cremation or burial services.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          M.  &quot;Primary
Legally Responsible Representative&quot; means a legally responsible
representative having the right to control the disposition of the remains of
the decedent, pursuant to RCW 68.50.160; that is, only if, after due diligence,
no surviving spouse can be located may a surviving adult child of the decedent
serve as the primary legally responsible representative, and so on.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          N.  &quot;Unclaimed&quot;
means that a legally responsible person or other person, church organization or
other organization does not assume financial responsibility for disposition of
the body.  (Ord. 12938 § 1, 1997:  Ord. 11073 § 2, 1993).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>8.64.020  Policies.</b> 
The county will provide funding for the disposition of the unclaimed remains of
indigent persons who died in King County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Disposition of remains at
county expense will be by cremation except when the decedent cannot be
identified, as verified by the medical examiner, or when the medical examiner,
for purposes related to the work of the medical examiner's office, authorizes
burial in lieu of cremation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          Prior to
cremation or burial, the Funeral Director shall request authorization of
payment for the disposition of indigent remains from the manager, pursuant to
the procedures stated in K.C.C. 8.64.030.  Payment maximum shall be for
services rendered, not to exceed the following:</span></p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0
 style='margin-left:45.9pt;border-collapse:collapse'>
 <tr>
  <td width=34 valign=top style='width:25.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=294 valign=top style='width:220.5pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><u><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>SERVICE</span></u></p>
  </td>
  <td width=181 valign=top style='width:135.9pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><u><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>PAYMENT
  MAXIMUM</span></u></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=34 valign=top style='width:25.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>1.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=294 valign=top style='width:220.5pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Mortuary Functions Prior
  to Cremation</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=181 valign=top style='width:135.9pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$325.00</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=34 valign=top style='width:25.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>2.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=294 valign=top style='width:220.5pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Cremation</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=181 valign=top style='width:135.9pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$125.00</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=34 valign=top style='width:25.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>3.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=294 valign=top style='width:220.5pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Mortuary Functions Prior
  to Burial</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=181 valign=top style='width:135.9pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$350.00</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=34 valign=top style='width:25.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>4.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=294 valign=top style='width:220.5pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Burial Only</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=181 valign=top style='width:135.9pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$200.00</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=34 valign=top style='width:25.6pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>5.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=294 valign=top style='width:220.5pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Burial with Plot</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=181 valign=top style='width:135.9pt;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$600.00</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          The rates shall
be effective for deaths occurring between January 1 through December 31, 1998.
These rates shall change annually on January 1, based on the local Consumer
Price Index (CPI).  The office of financial management shall be responsible for
calculating and publishing such rate changes.  Every five years the rates shall
be reviewed for their appropriateness by the county council, beginning with the
rates for 2003.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          If other
resources for disposition of the remains are available to the Funeral Director
or become available at a later date, either from the decedent's personal
effects or from some other source, the Funeral Director shall credit or
reimburse the county, dollar for dollar, for payments authorized by the manager
pursuant to this chapter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          Disposition of
the unclaimed remains will be authorized by the primary legally responsible
representative(s) or, in the absence of such authorization, by the county
medical examiner.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>The manager may authorize
payment after disposition has taken place only if all of the following
conditions are met:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          1.  Immediate
disposition of the decedent's remains was required for public health reasons;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          2.  It was not
possible to apply before the cremation or burial was performed; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          3.  It is the
first working day following the cremation or burial.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          Multiple containers
(caskets) may be placed in one grave at the discretion of the cemetery
authority so long as otherwise permitted by law.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          Beginning in
1998 and as needed thereafter, King County will purchase, at the price of a
&quot;Burial with Plot&quot; as identified in this chapter, a cemetery plot to
be used for the burial of remains whose cremation was funded by King County and
for which no alternative instructions for disposition have been made, pursuant
to WAC 98-40-080 or WAC 308-48-760.  Each plot shall be purchased from a
cemetery within King County chosen at random by the manager from a list of
interested cemeteries.  (Ord. 12938 § 2, 1997:  Ord. 11073 § 3, 1993).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>8.64.030  Procedures.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.
Responsibilities of Funeral Director.  The Funeral Director shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  Determine
that the decedent was indigent;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Attempt,
with due diligence as determined by the manager, to locate a legally
responsible representative of the decedent to claim the remains;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  If one or
more legally responsible representatives of the decedent are located but are
unable to bear the costs of the disposition of the remains, request that an
affidavit be signed by the primary legally responsible representative(s)
stating that the cost of the disposition of the remains cannot be borne by the
legally responsible representatives and authorizing the county's procedure for
disposition;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.  If one or
more legally responsible representatives are located, or are known to exist,
but they refuse, either outright or by evasion, to assume responsibility for
disposition of the remains and any of the primary legally responsible
representatives refuses, either outright or by evasion, to sign the affidavit
described in Subsection A.3, the Funeral Director shall submit an affidavit
attesting to this;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.  Submit to
the manager all documentation required by this chapter or by the Seattle-King
County department of public health, including documentation of the inability of
legally responsible representatives to bear the cost of disposition of the remains,
in form satisfactory to the manager.  This documentation must be submitted
either prior to disposition or with further documentation to support
authorization of payment after disposition, pursuant to K.C.C. 8.64.020.  The
form and documentation may be submitted by facsimile transmission if such
transmission is followed by signed originals;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.  Perform
mortuary functions and provide for cremation or burial, as approved for payment
by the manager;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            7.  Submit an
itemized request for payment (invoice) to the manager.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Responsibilities
of the Crematory Authority.  The Crematory Authority shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  Receive
the remains for cremation, as requested by the Funeral Director and as
authorized by the primary legally responsible representative(s) or the Medical
Examiner;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Perform
the cremation and related services;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  Submit an
itemized request for payment (invoice) to the manager.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  Responsibilities
of the Cemetery Authority.  The Cemetery Authority shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  Receive
the remains for burial, as requested by the Funeral Director and as authorized
by the Medical Examiner;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Perform
the burial and related services;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  Submit an
itemized request for payment (invoice) to the manager.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  Responsibilities
of the medical examiner.  The King County medical examiner shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  In the
absence of authorization of the county's procedure by the primary legally
responsible representative(s), authorize disposition of the unclaimed indigent
remains by either cremation or burial;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Forward
authorization to the manager.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  Responsibilities
of the prevention division of the Seattle-King County department of public
health. The manager shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  Secure
authorization from the medical examiner for disposition of unclaimed remains;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Authorize
or deny payment for services on the Disposition of Indigent Remains Record Form
as soon as possible, determining the amount of county funds to be approved,
pursuant to K.C.C. 8.64.020;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  Process
invoices for payment within three working days of their receipt;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.  Distribute
copies of the completed Disposition of Unclaimed Indigent Remains Record Form
to the Funeral Director, Crematory Authority (if applicable), Cemetery
Authority (if applicable), client file in the vital statistics office and to
the department of public health fiscal section.  (Ord. 12938 § 3, 1997:  Ord.
11073 § 4, 1993).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>8.64.040  Right
of appeal.</b>  If payment to the Funeral Director or the Cemetery Authority is
denied by the manager, the Funeral Director, Crematory Authority or Cemetery
Authority may appeal to the manager of the prevention division of the
Seattle-King County department of public health.  (Ord. 12938 § 4, 1997:  Ord.
11073 § 5. 1993).</span></p>

</div>

</body>

